        ['name' => 'Weather and data feeds', 'text' => 'Forecasts from MET Norway (free, no key needed) or Open-Meteo (which asks for its own key for commercial shows), and tickers from RSS, Atom, CSV and calendar feeds.'],
        ['name' => 'HTTP and TCP control', 'text' => 'A one-line-per-command TCP protocol and an HTTP API, with live state feedback, for integrators and any controller.'],
    ],

    'ai' => [
        'title' => 'An assistant that drafts, and you approve',
        'text' => 'Describe the day and the assistant drafts the screens, looks, cues and lower thirds for you. Nothing changes until you press APPLY, and what you apply lands in the preview, never on air. It is optional: everything else in Patterns works without it.',
        'items' => [
            'Describe the day (the screens, the schedule, the overlays you want) and it proposes planned screens, looks, a timed cue stack and lower thirds in the brand\'s colours.',
            'Attach the brief, a running order, photos of the rig, or PDF, Word and PowerPoint files, up to ten at a time. A running order becomes timed cues.',
            'Nothing changes until a person presses APPLY, and applied proposals land in the preview for you to check before you take them.',
            'It reads the live desk, so it will not propose what already exists, and it can explain why a cue ran late from the desk\'s own measurements.',
            'Ask about any item from its right-click menu, with that item\'s details already included.',
            'In audience play, it can take the first look at what the room writes, passing what is plainly fine and leaving the doubtful to the host.',
            'Link Patterns to a StageWatch approval desk and a person approves the assistant\'s proposals there before they reach Patterns.',
            'It sticks to Patterns and live-event AV, and it never sees passcodes or keys.',
            'Needs an internet connection and your own Anthropic API key, kept on that machine and never inside a show file.',
        ],
    ],

    'requirements' => [
        ['label' => 'Windows', 'value' => 'Windows 10 or Windows 11, 64-bit (x64).'],
        ['label' => 'Install', 'value' => 'None. One portable app with its own runtime built in. No admin rights needed to run it.'],
        ['label' => 'Graphics', 'value' => 'Patterns picks the strongest graphics card automatically and adapts its effects to the machine. Super Check rates the PC for the size of show.'],
        ['label' => 'Video playback and streaming', 'value' => 'Choose the full download, which includes the video engine, or install 64-bit VLC media player. Images work with either download.'],
        ['label' => 'NDI', 'value' => 'The free NDI Runtime. Without it Patterns runs normally, with NDI switched off.'],
        ['label' => 'Web pages', 'value' => 'Microsoft Edge WebView2, which comes with Windows 10 and 11.'],
        ['label' => 'PowerPoint, Keynote and Impress', 'value' => 'The free LibreOffice, installed or as a portable copy beside Patterns. PDF decks need nothing extra.'],
        ['label' => 'Stream Deck', 'value' => 'A Stream Deck with Bitfocus Companion 5 and the Patterns module.'],
        ['label' => 'Spotify break music', 'value' => 'Spotify Premium and your own free Spotify Client ID.'],
        ['label' => 'A second computer (optional)', 'value' => 'For a twin on another PC, a show caller\'s station, a stage timer machine or an audience hub out front, each running Patterns. The built-in Help shows how to start each one and link it to the desk. An automatic takeover between two PCs also needs a video switcher that confirms its commands.'],
        ['label' => 'Audience play', 'value' => 'Off until you switch it on. Phones join over the venue\'s Wi-Fi on a port of its own, with nothing to install.'],
        ['label' => 'AI assistant (optional)', 'value' => 'An internet connection and your own Anthropic API key.'],
    ],

    'getting_started' => [
        ['title' => 'Download Patterns', 'text' => 'Download Patterns from the client portal. Choose the full download if your show plays or streams video.'],
        ['title' => 'Put it anywhere and open it', 'text' => 'Save it to any folder you can write to, such as a USB stick or the desktop (unzip the full download first), and open Patterns. There is nothing to install and no admin rights are needed.'],
        ['title' => 'Arrange your screens', 'text' => 'On SETUP → Screens, drag displays together to make one canvas, press IDENTIFY (Shift+F7) to flash their numbers, and give each screen its role.'],
        ['title' => 'Build a picture in the preview', 'text' => 'Choose a pattern or some content from the Library. EDIT SAFE is on from the start, so it builds in the PREVIEW while the room sees nothing.'],
        ['title' => 'Take it to air', 'text' => 'Press TAKE for a transition or CUT for an instant change, then OUTPUTS ON (Shift+F5) to open the screens.'],
        ['title' => 'Save looks and build your cues', 'text' => 'Save looks on PLAN → Looks and recall them on F1 to F12. Build the cue stack on PLAN → Cues, or import the running order from Excel or CSV.'],
        ['title' => 'Check the machine before doors', 'text' => 'Open ADMIN → Machine, run Super Check, plug in the charger and turn on the show lock.'],
        ['title' => 'Run the show', 'text' => 'Run it from the Show panel or the RUN layout, or from a phone, tablet or Stream Deck set up on SETUP → Remote.'],
    ],

    'troubleshooting' => [
        ['q' => 'Nothing appears on my screens', 'a' => 'Check that the header shows SHOW, not PREP, because PREP holds the outputs closed. Then press OUTPUTS ON (Shift+F5), and make sure the screen is switched on in SETUP → Screens.'],
        ['q' => 'I changed something and the audience did not see it', 'a' => 'That is EDIT SAFE doing its job: edits build in the preview until you press TAKE or CUT. Things you fire, such as looks, cues, stingers and remote commands, go straight to air.'],
        ['q' => 'A display is missing from the Screens page', 'a' => 'Check that Windows shows the display in its own display settings, as a display of its own rather than a copy of another. Patterns notices displays as they come and go: one that was unplugged is recognised when it returns and switched back on with everything programmed for it, and a new one is offered on SETUP → Screens as a stand-in for a missing screen or as a screen of its own.'],
        ['q' => 'Videos will not play or the stream will not start', 'a' => 'Video playback and streaming use the video engine. Use the full download, which includes it, or install 64-bit VLC media player and restart Patterns. Images always work.'],
        ['q' => 'NDI says the runtime was not found', 'a' => 'Install the free NDI Runtime from the NDI website, then restart Patterns. The NDI page shows what was found.'],
        ['q' => 'My phone or Stream Deck cannot connect', 'a' => 'Check that the device is on the same network as the show PC and that remote control is on in SETUP → Remote. Use the address and pairing token shown on that page, and allow Patterns through Windows Firewall for that network.'],
        ['q' => 'Audience phones cannot join', 'a' => 'Check that remote control and the audience listener are both on in SETUP → Remote, and that the phones are on a Wi-Fi network that can reach the machine hosting the room. If the venue\'s Wi-Fi puts every phone behind one address, set the audience Network to Venue NAT on the same page. The room\'s status says when joins were refused from one address.'],
        ['q' => 'A PowerPoint deck looks different on screen', 'a' => 'Patterns turns each slide into a still page through LibreOffice, so animations do not play and a missing font is replaced. Install the deck\'s fonts on the show PC and check the deck once before the show. For a deck that needs its animations, show it with PowerPoint for the web as a web page.'],
        ['q' => 'A web video is not as smooth as expected', 'a' => 'The PAGE CONTROLS line shows the frame rate the room is actually getting. Set the page\'s Frames choice to Smooth, and on a laptop plug in the charger. If the rate stays low, press Copy support info on ADMIN → Machine and paste it into a support ticket.'],
        ['q' => 'A show file will not open', 'a' => 'Open ADMIN → Machine → Earlier versions of the show, choose the last good save and press RESTORE. Every save keeps the previous file and up to 20 timed copies.'],
        ['q' => 'The picture stutters on a laptop', 'a' => 'Plug in the charger and run Super Check on the Machine page, which shows the CPU, graphics, memory and frame rate with advice. Patterns uses the strongest graphics card and steps its effects down on smaller machines.'],
        ['q' => 'How do I send you the details of a problem?', 'a' => 'On ADMIN → Machine, press Copy support info and paste it into a support ticket in the client portal. For the full picture, SUPPORT BUNDLE on PLAN → Install saves the logs and settings as one file, with passwords and keys blanked out, ready to attach to the ticket.'],
    ],

    'faqs' => [
        ['q' => 'Is Patterns just a test pattern generator?', 'a' => 'No, though it still draws a rather good test card. It also switches every screen from a safe preview, plays slides, video and web pages, runs lower thirds, countdowns and sound, puts polls and quizzes from the audience\'s phones on the wall, and fires the show from a cue stack, a Stream Deck or a phone.'],
        ['q' => 'Does Patterns need installing?', 'a' => 'No. Patterns is one portable app for Windows 10 and 11 (64-bit). Run it from any folder you can write to, including a USB stick, with no admin rights. Settings, presets, brand kits and media live beside it, so copying the folder moves the whole show.'],
        ['q' => 'Can Patterns send test patterns over NDI?', 'a' => 'Yes. Patterns can run as many NDI senders as you need, each with its own name, size, frame rate and source, including 10-bit. It also receives NDI feeds as live inputs. NDI needs the free NDI Runtime.'],
        ['q' => 'How many projectors can Patterns blend?', 'a' => 'The Projection blend pattern lines up 2 to 12 projectors in a row or column. On the real outputs Patterns blends rows, stacks and grids such as 2×2 and 3×2, with gamma, black-level matching and mesh warp, and audits every join.'],
        ['q' => 'Does Patterns play PowerPoint?', 'a' => 'Yes. Patterns converts PowerPoint, Keynote and Impress files into pages in the background through the free LibreOffice, and PDF decks need nothing extra. The presenter\'s clicker turns the pages, and after the last page the next click can fire the next cue. For a deck that needs its animations, show it with PowerPoint for the web as a web page.'],
        ['q' => 'Can I run Patterns from a Stream Deck?', 'a' => 'Yes. Download the Patterns module, import it into Bitfocus Companion 5, pick your desk from the network and drag the presets onto your keys. Keys label themselves from your show and light up with live tally, and you can step through the desk\'s own menus on the deck to build the show from the keys.'],
        ['q' => 'Can I control Patterns from my phone?', 'a' => 'Yes. Turn on remote control in SETUP → Remote and open the address it shows on any phone or tablet on the same network, with nothing to install. The remote covers the show, cues, looks, screens, audio, lower thirds and overlays, and there are pages for the caller, the stage, the timer and the multiview, protected by a pairing token.'],
        ['q' => 'What happens if Patterns crashes mid-show?', 'a' => 'A watchdog restarts Patterns within seconds and puts back what the audience was watching, including the outputs, the lower third and the audio. For extra cover, a standby twin, as a second copy on the same machine or on a second computer running Patterns, keeps in step with the show, ready to take over.'],
        ['q' => 'Does Patterns need the internet?', 'a' => 'No. Patterns runs on the venue\'s own network. Only the optional AI assistant, Spotify, weather and online web pages or streams need an internet connection.'],
        ['q' => 'Can I build the show before I reach the venue?', 'a' => 'Yes. In PREP mode you plan screens at the venue\'s sizes and build every look and cue with the outputs held closed. At the venue, switch to SHOW and adopt each planned screen onto its real display.'],
        ['q' => 'Does Patterns work with StageWatch?', 'a' => 'Yes. They find each other on the local network. Patterns has a speaker countdown and messages to the stage of its own for a show without StageWatch; linked, its stage pages, a caller\'s station and a stage timer machine follow StageWatch\'s clock, so the room has one timer. StageWatch also counts down and controls Patterns\' video clips. The link uses StageWatch Pro or Production, and the clip countdown is part of StageWatch Production.'],
        ['q' => 'How is Patterns licensed?', 'a' => 'Patterns licences are coming soon. Patterns will follow the same one-off, offline licensing as StageWatch, with no licence server. See the Patterns licensing page to register your interest.'],
    ],

    'glossary' => [
        ['term' => 'Programme (PROGRAM)', 'definition' => 'What the audience sees now. Also called the air.'],
        ['term' => 'Preview (PREVIEW)', 'definition' => 'The next picture, being built. The audience does not see it.'],
        ['term' => 'EDIT SAFE', 'definition' => 'Keeps your edits in the preview until you take them to air. On by default.'],
        ['term' => 'TAKE and CUT', 'definition' => 'Move the preview to air with a transition (TAKE) or instantly (CUT).'],
        ['term' => 'SEND', 'definition' => 'Stages the preview on one screen\'s tile, so that screen\'s own CUT or TAKE puts it up there alone.'],
        ['term' => 'Look', 'definition' => 'A saved picture (pattern, per-screen pictures, overlays, countdown) you can recall, for example on an F-key.'],
        ['term' => 'Cue stack', 'definition' => 'The caller\'s running order. Each cue holds one or more actions and is run with GO.'],
        ['term' => 'Clicker list', 'definition' => 'A list a presenter steps through with a USB clicker, using Page Down and Page Up.'],
        ['term' => 'ARM, HOLD and STOP ALL', 'definition' => 'ARM enables GO, HOLD pauses the stack, and STOP ALL stops sounds and clips without touching the screens.'],
        ['term' => 'VT clock', 'definition' => 'The time left on the clip on air, with OUT IN 7 over its last ten seconds.'],
        ['term' => 'Pre-roll', 'definition' => 'The standby cue\'s clip opened and held ready, so GO cuts straight onto it.'],
        ['term' => 'Stage timer', 'definition' => 'The speaker\'s countdown on a confidence monitor or any browser: green, then amber and red at the times you set (two minutes and one by default), then counting how far over in red.'],
        ['term' => 'Message to stage', 'definition' => 'Words for the speaker or the crew, acknowledged on the stage page so the desk knows they were seen.'],
        ['term' => 'Caller\'s station', 'definition' => 'A second computer running Patterns as the show caller\'s own desk, with no outputs, linked to the main desk to call GO, STANDBY and HOLD.'],
        ['term' => 'Stage timer machine', 'definition' => 'A second computer running Patterns whose screen is the stage display, on the desk\'s clock.'],
        ['term' => 'CLOCKS APART', 'definition' => 'A warning that two machines\' own clocks differ by more than two seconds.'],
        ['term' => 'Canvas', 'definition' => 'Two or more screens joined into one picture.'],
        ['term' => 'Screen roles', 'definition' => 'Main, Confidence (stage monitor), Info (foyer screen) and Repeater (mirrors another screen).'],
        ['term' => 'OWN and LOCK', 'definition' => 'OWN gives a screen a picture of its own. LOCK keeps a screen\'s picture through looks and cues.'],
        ['term' => 'PREP, SHOW and RUN', 'definition' => 'PREP builds with the outputs held closed, SHOW lets the outputs open, and RUN is the caller\'s layout.'],
        ['term' => 'Planned screen and Adopt', 'definition' => 'A screen you plan before the hardware is there. Adopt maps it onto the real display at the venue.'],
        ['term' => 'Show panel', 'definition' => 'The one-page control surface for looks, the clicker, VOGs, stingers and audio.'],
        ['term' => 'Multiview', 'definition' => 'A monitor wall of programme, preview, screens, inputs and a clock, with tally.'],
        ['term' => 'Tally', 'definition' => 'The colour that says a source\'s state: red is on air, green or amber is in preview or held, grey is off.'],
        ['term' => 'VOG', 'definition' => '"Voice of God": a one-press announcement that ducks the music.'],
        ['term' => 'Stinger', 'definition' => 'A transition hit: a video clip, or a built-in effect sting that needs no file.'],
        ['term' => 'DUCK', 'definition' => 'Lowers music and clips while someone speaks in the room.'],
        ['term' => 'Lower third', 'definition' => 'A name and title graphic, designed in the built-in lower-thirds designer.'],
        ['term' => 'People library', 'definition' => 'Speakers\' names, roles and photos, ready for lower thirds.'],
        ['term' => 'Brand kit', 'definition' => 'A client\'s colours and logo, used across overlays and effects.'],
        ['term' => 'Test card', 'definition' => 'The Patterns line-up chart for pixels, overscan, levels and gamma.'],
        ['term' => 'Signal contract', 'definition' => 'What a screen\'s link should carry (resolution, exact rate, colour and connector), checked against what the display, Windows and the far end report.'],
        ['term' => 'Planned EDID', 'definition' => 'An EDID file Patterns builds from a signal contract, for a processor input or a PC\'s port.'],
        ['term' => 'Commissioning', 'definition' => 'Seven stages from discovering the displays to a known good rig, each judged from the rig\'s own evidence.'],
        ['term' => 'Known good', 'definition' => 'A saved record of the working rig, compared at each start.'],
        ['term' => 'Edge blend', 'definition' => 'Fading overlapping projectors so they read as one picture.'],
        ['term' => 'Black level', 'definition' => 'Lifts dark areas so projector overlaps look even on black.'],
        ['term' => 'Mesh warp', 'definition' => 'A grid of points you drag to fit a curved or awkward surface.'],
        ['term' => 'Bezels and gaps', 'definition' => 'Where a wall has no pixels, so content spans the physical wall correctly.'],
        ['term' => 'MIDI LEARN', 'definition' => 'Maps the next pad or fader you touch on a MIDI surface to a command chosen from a right-click menu.'],
        ['term' => 'Super Check', 'definition' => 'A one-button health check of the machine and the show, with a show-size rating.'],
        ['term' => 'The Eye (God\'s Eye)', 'definition' => 'A live map of the whole show (screens, sources, devices, audio and the other apps) with problems first.'],
        ['term' => 'REPLAY', 'definition' => 'Plays the show log back over the Eye\'s map, to see what happened at any moment.'],
        ['term' => 'Watchdog', 'definition' => 'Restarts Patterns after a crash or a hang and puts the show back.'],
        ['term' => 'Twin', 'definition' => 'A second Patterns, on the same machine or another computer, kept in step as a hot standby that can take over and hand back.'],
        ['term' => 'Show lock', 'definition' => 'Holds off notifications, other apps\' sounds, sleep and pop-ups during the show, and puts them back afterwards.'],
        ['term' => 'Show file', 'definition' => 'The whole rig and show saved as one file that travels with you.'],
        ['term' => 'Pairing token', 'definition' => 'The key a phone, remote or Stream Deck presents before it can control the desk.'],
        ['term' => 'Audience play', 'definition' => 'Polls, word clouds and timed quizzes from the audience\'s phones, joined from a room code or QR, with results and a leaderboard on the wall.'],
        ['term' => 'Arcade', 'definition' => 'Pong, Snake and Breakout on the big screen, played with phones, game pads or a Stream Deck.'],
        ['term' => 'Show network', 'definition' => 'How Patterns, StageWatch, AGMessage and PlayMap find each other and work together on the venue network.'],
    ],

